cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use DantinoX in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "DantinoX: One JAX/Flax Backbone for Autoregressive, Discrete-Diffusion, and Flow-Matching Language Models"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Simoni
    given-names: Marco
repository-code: "https://github.com/winstonsmith1897/DantinoX"
url: "https://dantinox.readthedocs.io"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - jax
  - flax
  - language-model
  - autoregressive
  - discrete-diffusion
  - flow-matching
  - transformer
abstract: >-
  DantinoX is a JAX/Flax library that trains and serves autoregressive,
  discrete-diffusion (LLaDA-style), and continuous flow-matching (ELF recipe)
  language models on a single shared transformer backbone — switching paradigm
  is a single config field. It includes multi-paradigm profiling, Fast-dLLM
  block-wise decoding with DualCache, LoRA fine-tuning, and text-embedder
  training.
